IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 803 of 2018
CITATION: (2018) 8 SCC 165
YEAR: 2018

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: J. Chelameswar, Sanjay Kishan Kaul

PARTIES:
Kishan Rao vs Shankargouda

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 138 NI Act, Section 139 NI Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
standard of proof, preponderance of probability, rebuttal of presumption

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Affirmed that the accused may rebut presumption under Section 139 NI Act through preponderance of probabilities, but a mere bald denial of liability is insufficient.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 138 NI Act, Section 139 NI Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

